{"ok": true, "result": [["BASE", "This dataset stores the experiment-level evaluation summary for the DistilBERT max-pooling cosine-similarity approach on the GLUE MRPC validation set. It contains a single summary record with three fields: accuracy (float), f1 (float), and classification_report (string). The values are computed by comparing binary paraphrase predictions—generated by thresholding cosine similarity between max-pooled DistilBERT embeddings of sentence pairs—against the ground-truth MRPC labels. In this workflow, the dataset serves as the final aggregated results table for the notebook, capturing overall model performance in a compact form for later inspection, comparison, and lineage tracking back to the validation data and prediction outputs.", "distilbert_max_pool_cosine_mrpc_summary", "record_list"], ["BASE", "Summary dataset for the DistilBERT cosine-similarity MRPC validation experiment. It contains an aggregate evaluation record for paraphrase detection on the GLUE MRPC validation split, where sentence1 and sentence2 are encoded with distilbert-base-uncased, the last 4 hidden layers are averaged, mean pooled into sentence embeddings, and classified by cosine similarity using a threshold of 0.85. The dataset structure has 3 fields: accuracy (float), f1 (float), and classification_report (string with per-class precision/recall/F1 and support). In this workflow, it serves as the final experiment-level metrics table summarizing model performance over the full validation set, with provenance linked to both the source dataset glue_mrpc_validation and the per-example prediction dataset cosine_mrpc_mean_similarity_prediction.", "distilbert_last4_mean_cosine_mrpc_summary", "record_list"], ["BASE", "distilbert_mean_cosine_median_threshold_mrpc_summary is a summary dataset containing the evaluation results for the DistilBERT mean-pooled cosine-similarity baseline on the GLUE MRPC validation set. It stores aggregate metrics computed after encoding each sentence pair with distilbert-base-uncased, measuring cosine similarity between the two sentence embeddings, and converting scores to binary paraphrase predictions using the median similarity as the decision threshold. The dataset has three fields: accuracy (float), f1 (float), and classification_report (string with per-class precision/recall/F1 and support). In this workflow, it serves as the final experiment-level output that summarizes model performance over the full validation split, with provenance linked to both the source dataset glue_mrpc_validation and the per-example prediction dataset threshold_cosine_mrpc_similarity_prediction.", "distilbert_mean_cosine_median_threshold_mrpc_summary", "record_list"], ["BASE", "Summary record list for the MRPC validation evaluation of a threshold-based paraphrase detection workflow using sentence-transformers/all-distilroberta-v1. This dataset contains experiment-level metrics computed by comparing predicted paraphrase labels from cosine similarity scores between sentence1 and sentence2 embeddings against the ground-truth labels in glue_mrpc_validation. Its structure is a record list with three fields: accuracy (float), f1 (float), and classification_report (string containing the full per-class evaluation report). In this notebook, it serves as the final aggregated result of the process, linking the full GLUE MRPC validation set and the generated prediction record list into a compact summary of model performance for the chosen cosine threshold.", "st_all_distilroberta_v1_cosine_threshold_mrpc_summary", "record_list"], ["BASE", "Summary dataset for the MRPC validation run using distilbert-base-uncased sentence embeddings. It contains aggregate evaluation results for paraphrase prediction on glue_mrpc_validation, where sentence1 and sentence2 are encoded separately, token embeddings are mean-pooled while excluding special tokens ([CLS], [SEP]), cosine similarity is computed between the two sentence embeddings, and a fixed threshold of 0.85 is used to produce binary paraphrase predictions.

